  user_input {
    user_response: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can  hotlink images from the html SASALLE HOTEL \342\200\224 Luxury Web + Mobile System (from Google Stitch Design)\n\nYou are Claude Opus 4.7 acting as a senior principal product engineer + UX architect + luxury hospitality system designer.\n\nYou are building a production-ready implementation based on an existing Google Stitch design file (provided in context).\n\n\360\237\217\233\357\270\217 OBJECTIVE\n\nTransform the Stitch design into a fully functional, production-grade luxury hotel system for:\n\nSASALLE HOTEL\n\nLocation: Batam, Indonesia\n\nThis is NOT a normal website build.\n\nThis is a luxury digital hospitality ecosystem inspired by:\n\nAman Resorts\nBulgari Hotels\nCheval Blanc\nRitz-Carlton Reserve\nFrench boutique architecture systems\n\360\237\247\240 CORE TASK\n\nUsing the Stitch design as source of truth:\n\nRebuild ALL UI into clean production-grade components\nPreserve layout fidelity, spacing, and hierarchy\nUpgrade design to ultra-luxury French European standard\nImprove micro-interactions and UX flow\nConvert into scalable system architecture (web + mobile-ready)\n\360\237\216\250 DESIGN ENHANCEMENT RULES (IMPORTANT)\n\nWhile preserving Stitch structure:\n\nYou MUST upgrade visual quality to:\nFrench editorial luxury aesthetic\nArchitectural minimalism\nHigh-end hospitality UI system\nApply SASALLE material identity:\nCharcoal Black (#0B0D10)\nDeep Brick Red (#7A3A2E)\nWarm Terracotta (#A0523D)\nSoft Ivory (#F5F1EA)\nMuted Gold (#B89B5E)\nSmoke Grey (#A7A7A7)\nHijau Nyonya Green (heritage accent)\nClay Roster Brown (architectural material tone)\n\360\237\247\261 ARCHITECTURAL DESIGN LANGUAGE\n\nDigitally represent:\n\nBrick fa\303\247ade elegance\nMatte black structural rhythm\nTerracotta warmth interiors\nHijau Nyonya green heritage accents\nClay roster stair textures (IMPORTANT \342\200\224 used in UI patterning, dividers, and structural motifs)\n\nUI must feel like:\n\na luxury architectural magazine, not a website\n\n\360\237\223\261 MOBILE-FIRST REQUIREMENT (CRITICAL)\n\nEverything must be optimized for:\n\niOS (safe areas, gesture navigation)\nAndroid (material soft transitions)\nThumb-first interaction design\n\nRules:\n\n3-step max booking flow\nBottom navigation minimal\nGesture-driven UX\nFull-screen imagery priority\nNo clutter\n\360\237\214\220 SYSTEM FEATURES (IMPLEMENT ALL)\nBooking System\nReal-time availability\nSeasonal pricing logic\nPackage bundling\nPromo code system\nCancellation rules UI\nGuest Experience\nPre-arrival preferences\nConcierge chat system (AI + human hybrid)\nAirport transfer booking\nIn-room dining system\nHousekeeping requests\nMobile App Features\nMobile check-in/out\nDigital room key concept\nLoyalty tiers (Silver / Gold / Black)\nSaved guest preferences\nPush notifications (minimal luxury tone)\nAdmin System\nRoom management\nBooking dashboard\nGuest CRM\nRevenue analytics\nOTA integration readiness (Booking.com / Agoda / Traveloka)\n\360\237\214\215 MULTILINGUAL SYSTEM\n\nFully implement:\n\nEnglish (default)\nBahasa Indonesia\nMandarin (Simplified Chinese)\n\nRules:\n\nFull UI translation (not partial)\nCultural adaptation of tone\nNo layout shift between languages\n\360\237\223\270 IMAGE / VISUAL RULES\n\nIf generating or selecting images:\n\nONLY use:\n\nLuxury European boutique hotels\nFrench architectural interiors\nHigh-end spa / dining / suite photography\nTerracotta + green heritage tones aligned with SASALLE\n\nMUST include:\n\nElegant hotel rooms\nArchitectural staircases (clay roster inspired)\nMinimal luxury bathrooms\nCinematic hotel exterior shots\n\nDO NOT use:\n\nCheap hotels\nGeneric stock photos\nOverly modern corporate hotels\nCartoon / CGI toy aesthetics\n\360\237\247\251 ENGINEERING OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\n\nGenerate:\n\n1. Production-ready frontend architecture\nComponent structure\nPage structure\nRouting system\n2. UI component system\nButtons\nCards\nBooking modules\nCalendar UI\nRoom selectors\n3. Full responsive system\nMobile / tablet / desktop breakpoints\nAdaptive layout rules\n4. Mobile app structure (React Native or Flutter concept)\nScreens\nNavigation flow\nState management approach\n5. UX flows\nBooking journey\nCheck-in flow\nConcierge flow\n\360\237\247\276 COPYWRITING STYLE\n\nUse:\n\nMinimal luxury tone\nArchitectural phrasing\nNo marketing exaggeration\n\nExamples:\n\n\342\200\234A quiet sanctuary shaped by proportion and light.\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Where European restraint meets tropical material heritage.\342\200\235\n\342\200\234A study in silence, texture, and form.\342\200\235\n\360\237\217\201 FINAL GOAL\n\nThe final output must feel like:\n\nA luxury hotel operating system\nA French boutique digital experience\nA high-end architectural interface product\n\nNOT a website.\n\nNOT a template.\n\nA world-class hospitality digital ecosystem.\n\n\342\232\241 IMPORTANT INSTRUCTION\n\nStrictly follow Stitch design structure first.\nThen elevate it to luxury SASALLE standard without breaking layout logic."
    items {
      text: "Build me an app with screens that look like this. You can  hotlink images from the html SASALLE HOTEL \342\200\224 Luxury Web + Mobile System (from Google Stitch Design)\n\nYou are Claude Opus 4.7 acting as a senior principal product engineer + UX architect + luxury hospitality system designer.\n\nYou are building a production-ready implementation based on an existing Google Stitch design file (provided in context).\n\n\360\237\217\233\357\270\217 OBJECTIVE\n\nTransform the Stitch design into a fully functional, production-grade luxury hotel system for:\n\nSASALLE HOTEL\n\nLocation: Batam, Indonesia\n\nThis is NOT a normal website build.\n\nThis is a luxury digital hospitality ecosystem inspired by:\n\nAman Resorts\nBulgari Hotels\nCheval Blanc\nRitz-Carlton Reserve\nFrench boutique architecture systems\n\360\237\247\240 CORE TASK\n\nUsing the Stitch design as source of truth:\n\nRebuild ALL UI into clean production-grade components\nPreserve layout fidelity, spacing, and hierarchy\nUpgrade design to ultra-luxury French European standard\nImprove micro-interactions and UX flow\nConvert into scalable system architecture (web + mobile-ready)\n\360\237\216\250 DESIGN ENHANCEMENT RULES (IMPORTANT)\n\nWhile preserving Stitch structure:\n\nYou MUST upgrade visual quality to:\nFrench editorial luxury aesthetic\nArchitectural minimalism\nHigh-end hospitality UI system\nApply SASALLE material identity:\nCharcoal Black (#0B0D10)\nDeep Brick Red (#7A3A2E)\nWarm Terracotta (#A0523D)\nSoft Ivory (#F5F1EA)\nMuted Gold (#B89B5E)\nSmoke Grey (#A7A7A7)\nHijau Nyonya Green (heritage accent)\nClay Roster Brown (architectural material tone)\n\360\237\247\261 ARCHITECTURAL DESIGN LANGUAGE\n\nDigitally represent:\n\nBrick fa\303\247ade elegance\nMatte black structural rhythm\nTerracotta warmth interiors\nHijau Nyonya green heritage accents\nClay roster stair textures (IMPORTANT \342\200\224 used in UI patterning, dividers, and structural motifs)\n\nUI must feel like:\n\na luxury architectural magazine, not a website\n\n\360\237\223\261 MOBILE-FIRST REQUIREMENT (CRITICAL)\n\nEverything must be optimized for:\n\niOS (safe areas, gesture navigation)\nAndroid (material soft transitions)\nThumb-first interaction design\n\nRules:\n\n3-step max booking flow\nBottom navigation minimal\nGesture-driven UX\nFull-screen imagery priority\nNo clutter\n\360\237\214\220 SYSTEM FEATURES (IMPLEMENT ALL)\nBooking System\nReal-time availability\nSeasonal pricing logic\nPackage bundling\nPromo code system\nCancellation rules UI\nGuest Experience\nPre-arrival preferences\nConcierge chat system (AI + human hybrid)\nAirport transfer booking\nIn-room dining system\nHousekeeping requests\nMobile App Features\nMobile check-in/out\nDigital room key concept\nLoyalty tiers (Silver / Gold / Black)\nSaved guest preferences\nPush notifications (minimal luxury tone)\nAdmin System\nRoom management\nBooking dashboard\nGuest CRM\nRevenue analytics\nOTA integration readiness (Booking.com / Agoda / Traveloka)\n\360\237\214\215 MULTILINGUAL SYSTEM\n\nFully implement:\n\nEnglish (default)\nBahasa Indonesia\nMandarin (Simplified Chinese)\n\nRules:\n\nFull UI translation (not partial)\nCultural adaptation of tone\nNo layout shift between languages\n\360\237\223\270 IMAGE / VISUAL RULES\n\nIf generating or selecting images:\n\nONLY use:\n\nLuxury European boutique hotels\nFrench architectural interiors\nHigh-end spa / dining / suite photography\nTerracotta + green heritage tones aligned with SASALLE\n\nMUST include:\n\nElegant hotel rooms\nArchitectural staircases (clay roster inspired)\nMinimal luxury bathrooms\nCinematic hotel exterior shots\n\nDO NOT use:\n\nCheap hotels\nGeneric stock photos\nOverly modern corporate hotels\nCartoon / CGI toy aesthetics\n\360\237\247\251 ENGINEERING OUTPUT REQUIREMENTS\n\nGenerate:\n\n1. Production-ready frontend architecture\nComponent structure\nPage structure\nRouting system\n2. UI component system\nButtons\nCards\nBooking modules\nCalendar UI\nRoom selectors\n3. Full responsive system\nMobile / tablet / desktop breakpoints\nAdaptive layout rules\n4. Mobile app structure (React Native or Flutter concept)\nScreens\nNavigation flow\nState management approach\n5. UX flows\nBooking journey\nCheck-in flow\nConcierge flow\n\360\237\247\276 COPYWRITING STYLE\n\nUse:\n\nMinimal luxury tone\nArchitectural phrasing\nNo marketing exaggeration\n\nExamples:\n\n\342\200\234A quiet sanctuary shaped by proportion and light.\342\200\235\n\342\200\234Where European restraint meets tropical material heritage.\342\200\235\n\342\200\234A study in silence, texture, and form.\342\200\235\n\360\237\217\201 FINAL GOAL\n\nThe final output must feel like:\n\nA luxury hotel operating system\nA French boutique digital experience\nA high-end architectural interface product\n\nNOT a website.\n\nNOT a template.\n\nA world-class hospitality digital ecosystem.\n\n\342\232\241 IMPORTANT INSTRUCTION\n\nStrictly follow Stitch design structure first.\nThen elevate it to luxury SASALLE standard without breaking layout logic."
