  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Project Needs**\n\nI\'m currently assessing the skills and files related to the SASALLE HOTEL project in Batam. My initial focus is on the feasibility of integrating Firebase. This review is critical to ensure we can build a production-grade web and mobile system for a luxury hotel.\n\n\n**Considering Local Database Approach**\n\nI\'m now diving into the potential for a local database solution. Given the project\'s requirements for booking, real-time availability, and CRM features, I am carefully considering the tradeoffs of using a local state engine instead of Firebase. I\'m focusing on `/package.json` to inform my decision, and I am especially cautious about external dependencies. I intend to build a full backend/frontend split if necessary.\n\n\n**Integrating Gemini API**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to integrating the Gemini API for the concierge chat system, aiming for an AI + human hybrid approach. I\'m keen on a full-stack Express + Vite server setup with server-side API calls. This includes a custom Express server that handles Gemini API requests. I\'m going to determine if the `gemini-api` skill is the best fit.\n\n\n**Verifying Gemini Skill Relevance**\n\nI\'m now cross-referencing the available skills list to confirm `gemini-api` is the best approach, checking `skills/system_skills/gemini_api/SKILL.md` for a deeper understanding. The AI concierge chatbot feature makes this highly relevant. I\'m also briefly considering `google-maps-platform` for Batam maps, although I think customized maps are better. Finally, I\'m noting the potential of `image-generation` for luxury interior visuals.\n\n\n**Confirming Path Validity**\n\nI\'m now verifying the exact file path for the Gemini API skill. It seems there was a moment of doubt, so I double-checked the documentation. The path seems correct. I also glanced at the provided images to confirm that the file does, indeed, exist.\n\n\n**Evaluating Image Data**\n\nI\'m now reviewing the image data to understand its relevance to the project. The links provided seem to point to profile images and other assets. My aim is to assess if these images are usable within the context of the SASALLE Hotel project.\n\n\n**Reviewing Image Assets**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the image assets provided. I see a few links; they appear to be profile images. I\'m assessing if they\'re applicable to the SASALLE Hotel project.\n\n\n"
