  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering Package Dependencies**\n\nI\'m presently evaluating potential dependencies. I\'m thinking about `@types/react`, and other relevant typing packages, but standard ones might suffice. I\'m also considering the use of React components for rendering markdown; that is a specific guideline. I prefer to utilize `react`.\n\n\n**Evaluating Markdown Rendering**\n\nI\'ve decided to install `react-markdown` for the rendering, just to stay compliant with the markdown guidelines. It\'s easy enough using `install_applet_package`. It simplifies the process and feels like the right call for safety and adherence. Now I\'m shifting focus to the Full-Stack Applications guidelines, specifically the necessary script updates in `package.json` if I make any custom server edits.\n\n\n**Defining Full-Stack Structure**\n\nI\'m now implementing the full-stack structure as specified. The server setup is great, handling both API and frontend. I\'m especially happy with the `tsx` hot-reloading for TypeScript server scripts, which improves development. I\'m focusing on the server with its \"dist/server.cjs\" entry point and start script.\n\nI\'m now starting to consider the functionality of the SASALLE hotel system. I\'m aiming for an elegant, architectural, and minimal design. I\'m thinking about the user flow. First, I\'m analyzing the screens in the designs. We\'ve got a rooms and suites page to start with.\n\n\n**Analyzing Room Data**\n\nI\'m now examining the provided room data. I am organizing details such as names, descriptions, and pricing. I am also working with image URLs. I intend to structure these data points for seamless integration into the application\'s room display. I will be incorporating these details into the rooms and suites page.\n\n\n**Designing Page Layouts**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the visual structure of the Spa & Wellness page. I\'m taking the architectural stillness theme to the layout. I\'m focusing on the cinematic hero section and curated experiences grid. My thoughts are focusing on the immersive feel.\n\n\n**Defining Page Content**\n\nI am now focusing on the content and images for the Spa & Wellness page. I\'m thinking about the \"Heritage Botanicals: The Hijau Nyonya Clay Wrap\" with its specific URL and imagery. I am also working on the design for the \"Reserve Your Moment\" call to action. I am also planning the cinematic hero image for the dining page, \"The Brick & Iron\".\n\n\n**Defining Home Page Content**\n\nI\'m now integrating content for the home page. The focus is on \"The Art of Deep Presence\" with the provided hero image URL. I\'m incorporating the editorial text, \"The Ritual of the Stay...\" and establishing the grid cards which emphasize the \"Craft: Material\" theme. I\'m considering \"Seasonal Manifestations\" with Earth, Metal, and Glass phases. Additionally, I am designing the \"Secure a Table\" section with horizontal scrolling.\n\n\n**Integrating Public Image URLs**\n\nI\'m now integrating the provided public image URLs. Specifically, I am using the image at `https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuCr4p6em0177fbmUi22y1r_j09M115Qc3c2mLjF70gMCGPLM49jbNZBrBZXN1eNkfk0SEVmsIbvU_yXtTHIUHQ5a-jOkEEwCEmHIJWmoqoNLX1o6OtLMQRO4O2GM-2Z5Q9kam3OSsVCUec47MtsnhghGSguAiZqRhNqVV9NoL6pATEYzYSHdSQ1hpS3i0U74UA7AlV4ejCKKFiqE6xcqZqs1_jnWQyi2f4ofnFkyObCd8vKMnfaGHq_OI8amMdJb_VcN9qfe6cSP1M-` for \"Honesty\" and `https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/aida-public/AB6AXuAMJOTaYWp6dwSyET66aApi6HbIoGxv9GqWnPaHAvUwnLMAABWv-X9cKglK4Alf9wHsB4vupu9CiWyEk4unTzHoJ5SdJYxUFzKABK-45C9VUysS5PvfHyYZYWhHKJPT9JPHD8PyX88DuP5172ZPO0P7huYzY9BX5qLSDS3Bkjo90WKawZuUO6jjvUp3hkqTKzCLuhjWQz41IhuDbEzt0lNPTW87J5o8ImC7zJHcr1EgVy7s6HwJigj9i8JyRuKyQO0NKycyCkEDvrwQ` for \"Space: The Quietude.\" I\'m now also considering the implementation of the Interactive components in the design.\n\n\n**Planning Multilingual Support**\n\nI\'m now integrating multilingual functionality, specifically English, Bahasa Indonesia, and Mandarin, which will require a system for dynamic text replacement. I am leaning towards a clean multi-view system for a stunning user experience. I\'m focusing on \"Guest View\" for desktop and mobile simulation with features like digital key and push notifications, and also a \"Back of House Admin\" view.\n\n\n**Defining Localization Structure**\n\nI\'m now establishing the localization dictionary structure and application state. I\'ve decided on a state variable to manage languages and create `src/types.ts` for declaring interfaces and variables. I am focusing on the comprehensive dictionary for preventing layout shifts. I am also determining the localization requirements for all screens.\n\n\n**Defining File Structure**\n\nI am now outlining the file structure to support modularity. I\'ve got `src/types.ts` for interfaces, `src/data.ts` for data, and components like Header, BottomNav, and GuestView planned. These will hold separate data and logic, as per guidelines. I\'m focusing on static data.\n\n\n**Designing Component Hierarchy**\n\nI\'m now outlining key React components. I\'m focusing on the AdminView for back-of-house data, a mobile frame emulator, and the concierge chat system connected to the backend Gemini API. I\'m also thinking about a streamlined booking wizard and digital key implementation. I\'m finalizing the structure to work with my `index.css` Tailwind configuration and server.\n\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 23
      nanos: 154721364
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
