  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Data Structure**\n\nI\'m currently structuring the `/src/data.ts` file. It will contain the rooms list with image links from the Stitch file. I\'m also preparing the localization dictionary to support English, Indonesian, and Chinese translations without layout shifts. Furthermore, the file will house promo items, dining options, initial bookings, and a list for custom preferences.\n\n\n**Adding Offline Support**\n\nI\'ve incorporated predefined responses to address offline scenarios or API failures with the Gemini API. These responses will ensure users aren\'t left hanging. Currently, I\'m analyzing the Stitch file, focusing on images and textual descriptions for reference. For example, I\'m noting the descriptions and starting prices for the Heritage Suite and Obsidian Studio, along with their respective image URLs.\n\n\n**Expanding Data Scope**\n\nI\'m now incorporating details for \"The Ivory Pavilion\" and the \"Cinematic Hero Spa,\" pulling descriptions, starting prices, and image URLs. These will enhance our data structure. I\'m focusing on the elegant descriptions and high-quality images.\n\n\n**Incorporating Service Descriptions**\n\nI\'m now integrating descriptions and image URLs for specific services. I\'m adding details for \"The Stone Bathing Ritual\", \"The Hijau Nyonya Clay Wrap\", and \"The Brick & Iron Dining\", enriching our dataset with visual and textual information to ensure a comprehensive user experience.\n\n\n**Adding Visual References**\n\nI\'m now integrating new image URLs into the dataset. I\'ve added Lobby Art, a Travertine Stone Texture, and an image titled \"The Quietude Window Contrast\" to enhance the visual presentation of the data. I\'m carefully assigning these to relevant elements.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 39
      nanos: 917827100
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
